 a hands-on introduction to chair restoration and upholstery
A workshop guide to repairing a wooden chair: a hands-on introduction to chair restoration and upholstery
English | October 25, 2018 | ISBN-10: 1786273428 | 144 pages | PDF | 24.4 MB
Get hands-on experience in restoring a wooden chair with this expert guide. From identifying areas of damage to reupholstering the seat, this practical workshop guide is designed to help you learn the skills needed to restore a wooden chair to its former glory.
The book begins with an overview of the chair restoration process, covering common types of damage and the tools and materials needed to repair them. The following chapters guide you through the process of:
* Assessing the chair's condition and identifying areas that need attention
* Disassembling the chair and sorting components
* Repairing cracks, splits, and other damage to the wood
* Refinishing the wood to restore its original color and finish
* Reupholstering the seat and backrest with new fabric and padding
* Reassembling the chair and adding any finishing touches

Throughout the book, expert tips and tricks are shared, along with step-by-step instructions and photographs to help you complete each stage of the restoration process. Whether you're a beginner or an experienced woodworker, this comprehensive guide will give you the confidence to tackle even the most challenging chair restoration projects.
* A hands-on guide to restoring a wooden chair, covering all aspects of the process
* Step-by-step instructions and photographs help you complete each stage of the restoration
* Expert tips and tricks shared throughout the book
* A comprehensive guide that's perfect for beginners or experienced woodworkers
* Includes information on chair safety and how to prevent common mistakes while working on a chair
